\newlabel{fig:arch}{{1}{3}{Architecture of my-agent. The LLM drives every stage; modeling and evaluation iterate via tree search, invoking Auto-ML tools through the shell, while the experience library and experiment records close the evidence loop. Blue: the injection layer (Section~\ref {sec:v5}) --- the Stage 0.5 dossier emits typed operators that drive the external-data layer, whose data-level arms race against the no-external baseline.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Tree-search protocol.}{3}{section*.5}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The tree-search loop used in all my-agent runs of this report (22--80 nodes per competition). Each node is a complete, executable solution scored by local cross-validation; lineages are abandoned on plateau, and the budget phase machine forces one exploration burst before stopping. Blue: the injection layer's operator entry points (Section\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {sec:v5}) --- model-level operators seed starting nodes; data-level operators build separately raced arms.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tree}{{2}{4}{The tree-search loop used in all my-agent runs of this report (22--80 nodes per competition). Each node is a complete, executable solution scored by local cross-validation; lineages are abandoned on plateau, and the budget phase machine forces one exploration burst before stopping. Blue: the injection layer's operator entry points (Section~\ref {sec:v5}) --- model-level operators seed starting nodes; data-level operators build separately raced arms.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
