\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The 20-competition benchmark, state as of 2026-08-18. All cells are public/private leaderboard scores; \textbf  {bold} marks the best \emph  {private} score of the three (raw, direction-aware; the paired-test verdicts, which this raw reading does not replace, are in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:winrates}). my-agent's column comes from the credentialed operator scoring step of 2026-08-18; its percentile ranks await a leaderboard-snapshot pull. NVIDIA and AIDE cells are frozen leaderboard scores with percentile rank (PR) in parentheses. Lane status: 16 of 20 lanes complete and scored (${\sim }19$ hours of lane time); s6e2 running; tps-aug/jan/sep-2022 queued (TBD rows, not bolded). Right of the vertical rule, separated because it is \emph  {not comparable} to the leaderboard columns: each lane's own local CV (OOF) estimate, the lane's internal progress signal only (each lane chooses its own split scheme, and two lanes score on different metrics than their leaderboard).\relax }}{10}{table.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
